; Test: != operator (exclusion/all-different binding)
; ===================================================
;
; != generates ALL bindings where values are DIFFERENT
; Pattern: (!= <expr1> <expr2>) binds to all pairs where expr1 ≠ expr2

; Setup: Three values in space
(VAL X)
(VAL Y)
(VAL Z)

; Test: Find all pairs where values differ
; (!= (VAL $x) (VAL $y)) will bind:
;   $x=X, $y=Y
;   $x=X, $y=Z
;   $x=Y, $y=X
;   $x=Y, $y=Z
;   $x=Z, $y=X
;   $x=Z, $y=Y
; (6 combinations - all different pairs)

(exec 0
  (I (!= (VAL $x) (VAL $y)))
  (O (+ (OUT ($x != $y)))))

; Expected output (6 facts):
; (OUT (X != Y))
; (OUT (X != Z))
; (OUT (Y != X))
; (OUT (Y != Z))
; (OUT (Z != X))
; (OUT (Z != Y))
;
; Key insight: != is ALL-DIFFERENT generator, not equality check!
; It produces the cartesian product excluding equal pairs.
